      "content": "While some risk factors, such as family history and age, cannot be changed, there are steps you can take to help prevent or slow down the buildup of plaque. Maintaining a healthy lifestyle through diet, exercise, and stress management can help manage your LDL levels and increase your HDL levels, making your cardiovascular risk lower. Lifestyle modifications can include eating a heart-healthy diet, exercising regularly, quitting smoking, and limiting stress. It's also essential to work with your healthcare provider to develop a plan tailored to your individual needs.",
